//
// SmolVLA verify gate: end-to-end action-chunk regression, NPU SigLIP vision +
// connector against the unmodified lerobot CPU model, with fixed zero noise so
// the comparison is deterministic.
//
// SmolVLA emits a continuous action chunk rather than tokens, so this uses the
// regression gate from verify/comparators.py (cosine >= 0.99 AND normalized
// MSE <= 0.04) rather than the top-k token-set gate the autoregressive LLM
// siblings use.
//
// This example needs a heavier dependency set than the other LLM examples:
// torch + lerobot[dataset] + num2words, because it verifies against the
// upstream lerobot policy itself. To enable this test:
//
//   pip install -r programming_examples/llms/smolvla/requirements.txt
//
// installed into the interpreter that also has air + pyxrt, so the NPU stage
// runs in the same process as the model. Note that lerobot requires
// numpy>=2.0, which may upgrade numpy across a major version in a shared
// environment — see that requirements.txt for the caveat.
//
// Two features gate this beyond the usual ones. `lerobot` is added by
// lit.cfg.py when the package imports, so a runner without it reports
// UNSUPPORTED instead of failing on an ImportError.
// `hfweights_lerobot_smolvla_base` follows the sibling convention: lit.cfg.py
// scans the local HF cache and adds a feature per seeded repo, so this skips
// cleanly rather than trying to download 450M params on a cold cache. The
// compile test needs neither and carries no such REQUIRES.
//
// No fixture required: the gate computes its pure-CPU reference live,
// in-process, from the same policy object.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai_npu2, peano, hf_token, lerobot, hfweights_lerobot_smolvla_base
//
// RUN: mkdir -p test_peano_verify
// RUN: cd test_peano_verify
// RUN: make -f %S/Makefile verify PEANO_INSTALL_DIR=%PEANO_INSTALL_DIR | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: [verify] PASS
